  topicId: sinks
  title: Forests are carbon sinks
  body: 'Trees take in CO2 as they grow and store the carbon in their trunks, roots
    and the soil. That carbon stays out of the air only while the forest stands:
    when trees are cut and burned or left to rot, it returns to the atmosphere as
    CO2.'
